{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 66,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iraq, Kuwait, Bahrain, Qatar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3966,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7766,
    "dDurationMs": 4534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are literally built\ntheir entire economies on oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12766,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then to diversify to the risk,\nif you will,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15766,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they build some of the biggest airliners\nin the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19166,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they became a so-called safe\nhaven in the Middle East."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22833,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now this war\nand specifically the blockade of Hormuz"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28533,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are threatening\nall of it at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32700,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And honestly, I don't think people realize\nyet how unfathomably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36900,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big this crisis is for the Gulf economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40300,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, take Qatar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its economy depends on oil,\nand especially natural"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas for roughly 42%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51433,
    "dDurationMs": 2333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And almost all of that has to go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53766,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the Strait of Hormuz to de-risk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57333,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though Qatar became an international\nair travel hub,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61366,
    "dDurationMs": 5134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means now aviation accounts\nfor a little over 10%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67533,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of its economy and tourism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71133,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For another, roughly 10%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74733,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of GDP seemed very smart\njust a few months ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78866,
    "dDurationMs": 5567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now, with both its airspace\nand the strait close, it means that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84433,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least 62% of Qatar's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88966,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire\neconomy is in a state of total paralysis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93233,
    "dDurationMs": 5267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just for context, Ukraine's\neconomy contracted by roughly 30% in 2022."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98533,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US economy contracted for 29%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101433,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during the Great Depression\nover the course of four years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105666,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, Qatar is not Ukraine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107966,
    "dDurationMs": 2367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is one of the wealthiest countries\nin the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110333,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a month long shutdown was manageable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113733,
    "dDurationMs": 2367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the war ends in a month."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116100,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A Goldman Sachs economist has estimated\nthat Qatar's economy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119366,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will only contract by 14% in 2026."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126600,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, that is a substantially bigger\nrecession than happened during Covid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131100,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, like after Covid,\nQatar will bounce back from this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136100,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138166,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the thing is, this conflict, it\ndoesn't look like it's getting any better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142666,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, I've read some pretty\nalarming reports that Gulf states like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146566,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qatar depend for 99%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152266,
    "dDurationMs": 434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152700,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drinking water on these\nsix desalination plants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156566,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which have in Bahrain\nalready been targeted in the war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160633,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that in a true disaster\nscenario, the entire country"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164966,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may need to be evacuated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167766,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that raises the question are Gulf\neconomies facing a total collapse?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172966,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iran has said it wants U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174866,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "troops out of the Middle East."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176666,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could it soon forced Gulf economies\nto eject U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179866,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "troops simply by choking their economies?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183266,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, I'm Yuri, I'm a pizza in economics,\nand I've spent the last days analyzing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187633,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of the Gulf economies\nand how bad they will be affected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191533,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by three potential scenarios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194466,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scenario number one, a quick end\nto the war, either because the US wins are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200166,
    "dDurationMs": 4467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because Iran forces them to push out US\ntroops, the Gulf countries, that is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204866,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's scenario number two,\na long a war, in which case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208833,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've calculated\nhow long the various Gulf economies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211933,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can survive without export revenue\nthrough the Strait of Hormuz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215966,
    "dDurationMs": 4767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, scenario number three,\na disaster scenario"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220733,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which either the Gulf economies\nrun out of water or population"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225266,
    "dDurationMs": 4834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given that some rely\nfor almost 90% on immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230466,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's get into it\nwith scenario number one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234433,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A short war, which is exactly\nwhat we have been seeing so far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238766,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand the damage done so far,\nwe have to look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241766,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the two biggest disruptions\ndone to the Gulf countries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246400,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is exactly what we have seen so far\na short disruption."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251400,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to understand the damage\nthat has already been done, we have to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255600,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look at the two biggest disruptions\nthat to go of countries have faced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260566,
    "dDurationMs": 3934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, there's the stencil of industries\nthat depend on the Strait of Hormuz"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264500,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for exports, such as oil and gas\nand also manufacturing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269066,
    "dDurationMs": 4434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus the effective standstill of air\ntravel and tourism, oil and gas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273533,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far,\nBahrain is the least dependent on it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277866,
    "dDurationMs": 5634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with it\naccounting for roughly 26% of its economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283666,
    "dDurationMs": 1767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, its main diversification"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285433,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strategy has been manufacturing,\nwhich now accounts for roughly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290700,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "15% of its economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293966,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But sadly,\nthat is also mostly for exporting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300274,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bahrain is also a major\ntourist destination these days, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303108,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is mostly for local tourists,\nso that seems to be fine so far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307674,
    "dDurationMs": 7167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all in all, I'd say that roughly 41%\nof its economy is paralyzed right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315141,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Compare that to Kuwait,\nwhich depends for 35% on oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319408,
    "dDurationMs": 4733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and gas, while trade, tourism\nand manufacturing is relatively small."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324141,
    "dDurationMs": 6133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'd say that roughly 38% of its\neconomy is paralyzed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330741,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its northern neighbor, Iraq,\nit depends for about 55%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334674,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's\nquite a lot on oil and gas for its GDP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338241,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And almost all of that\nwas exported through her moose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341241,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now Iraq has just reopened its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345908,
    "dDurationMs": 2666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pipeline to Turkey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349774,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350374,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "help it divert about 20% of its oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353608,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at this very important, roughly double\nthe price as before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357508,
    "dDurationMs": 8066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for them, I'd say that\nroughly 33% of their economy is paralyzed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366141,
    "dDurationMs": 5767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much less than Qatar, which we've already\ndiscussed to be at 62%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372608,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now moving on to the big boy\nin the region, Saudi Arabia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376174,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It depends for roughly 34% on oil and gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380341,
    "dDurationMs": 5967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 33% on manufacturing\nand 8% on aviation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386308,
    "dDurationMs": 1866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And 5% on tourism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388174,
    "dDurationMs": 2067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, calculating\nhow much of Saudi Arabia's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390241,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economy is paralyzed\nis very difficult for two reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394008,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, much of their airspace,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396608,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tourist areas\nand many of their ports are actually open."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400108,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second,\nthey have a hugely important pipeline"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404908,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which allows them to export\nabout 60 to 70% of their oil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408774,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is more crucial than they think."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411374,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, because they are currently selling\nthat oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414641,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at almost double\nthe price than they were before the war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418908,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, there's the UAE, which depends\nfor roughly 24% on oil and gas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424408,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But like Saudi Arabia, it has a pipeline"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429508,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that has been estimated\nto help itself 43% of its oil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433574,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And again, because the prices\nare roughly double than that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436408,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were before the war,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437708,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it means that they roughly have the same\nrevenue from oil as they had before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442708,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But much like Bahrain and Saudi Arabia,\nthey have major manufacturing sector,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447141,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they also have a lot of mining,\nunlike these economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450908,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a lot of this is actually exposed\nto their biggest port being closed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456441,
    "dDurationMs": 1167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457608,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That being said, the UAE\nand especially of course Dubai relies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461908,
    "dDurationMs": 5166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heavily on aviation 18% and tourism 11%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467241,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which have both mostly been paralyzed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471574,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for these two countries\nis really anyone's guess."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474874,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But let's say\njust for the sake of argument, that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478674,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the UAE has 20% of its economy\nbeing paralyzed and Saudi Arabia ten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485174,
    "dDurationMs": 1567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, it's more in reality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486741,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but both of them are really profiting\nnow from much higher oil prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490708,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, stuff doesn't\njust go out through the Strait of Hormuz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495608,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the Gulf economies\nalso used the Strait of Hormuz"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499241,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for about 70% of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504141,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their crucial food and medicine imports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507974,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, after the main imports, ports"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511941,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as and I hope I'm going to pronounce\nthis correctly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515241,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qasr in Iraq"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519208,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the port in the city of Kuwait,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521908,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the port south of Doha, and especially,\nmost importantly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526741,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the port in Dubai known as Jebel Ali,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530874,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are essentially now shut down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533574,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now they have to rely for these imports on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537008,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "land routes via Jordan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541441,
    "dDurationMs": 2367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and via Saudi"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543808,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Arabia, and finally, of course, via"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547374,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ports of Fujairah in the UAE."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551641,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Qatar has largely started\nimporting via air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555708,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is much more expensive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557608,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the result of all of this,\nthese imports has been long traffic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561341,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jams at ports\nnot made for such high volumes of goods,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565408,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore a big spike\nin the cost of food and medicine imports."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569608,
    "dDurationMs": 2266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But crucially,\nbecause many Gulf governments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571874,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have prohibited\nsupermarkets from price gouging,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575108,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and because many of them have large food\nreserves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578874,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so far\nthe damage from this has been limited"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582541,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and consumer prices have not gone up\nby as much as you would have expected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587174,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these are, I think, the main"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589974,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pain points for the Gulf countries so far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593174,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of them are facing\nfar higher import costs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597841,
    "dDurationMs": 6367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for food and medicine,\nand a chaotic reshuffling of trade routes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605408,
    "dDurationMs": 2466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qatar and Kuwait."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607874,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Qatar and Kuwait\nhave been hit the hardest so far,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612941,
    "dDurationMs": 5633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while Saudi Arabia and to a lesser extent\nthe UAE have been doing fairly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618574,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "okay so far due to them\ngetting a much higher price for the oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623108,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is still being exported\nthrough their pipelines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627841,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And therefore, I think it makes sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629208,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Goldman Sachs economist\nFarouk Snoozer muddled in early March"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633641,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if the war ends late April,\nso fairly soon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637908,
    "dDurationMs": 4766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 2026 economies of Qatar\nand Kuwait will contract"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642674,
    "dDurationMs": 5667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both by roughly minus 14%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649474,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,\nthe UAE would only shrink by minus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653408,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5% in 2026 and Saudi"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656674,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Arabia by minus 3%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660974,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given what we've seen,\nI think Bahrain and Iraq will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664108,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then land somewhere\nin between these numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668608,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, all of that is very substantial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670408,
    "dDurationMs": 2666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a bigger hit than during Covid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673074,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But honestly, me as well as most analysts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675841,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think that this will be manageable\ngiven how rich these countries are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679674,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However,\nwill the war actually end late April?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683008,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That assumption is looking\nincreasingly unlikely, and this brings us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687341,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to scenario number two a long war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691541,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happens to the Gulf countries\nif the war last much longer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695508,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can Iran break their economies?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697708,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Historically, if we want to know whether\nor not a war economy will actually break."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702008,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What matters is not GDP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703541,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What matters is whether or not a country\ncan earn enough international currency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707841,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to finance its war efforts\nand more importantly, in this case, feed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712508,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713908,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, given that the Gulf countries\nare highly reliant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717508,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on crucial food and medicine imports,\nplus the fact that they may need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722208,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to import a lot of missiles\nand other defense systems in a long war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726808,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's safe to assume\nfor a worst case scenario, that they need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729974,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep importing\njust as many goods as before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734008,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So fewer luxury goods,\nbut more essential goods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737108,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But while Qatar, Bahrain and Kuwait's\neconomies may depend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743674,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the Strait of Hormuz for less than or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747474,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about half their GDP,\ntheir export revenues depend on it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751374,
    "dDurationMs": 4467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a whopping 95%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756141,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,\nIraq's northern pipeline now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758341,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means that it has about an exposure of 80%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761908,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it comes to export revenues."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765208,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, again, Saudi Arabia\nand the UAE are difficult to estimate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768808,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but thanks to their pipelines\nand the increased price of oil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772941,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially if there is a long war,\nfor simplicity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776674,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will assume that the Saudis only take a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780474,
    "dDurationMs": 2134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20% hit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783741,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the UAE takes a 30%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788141,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hit to their export to revenues."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791141,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I feel a lot, honestly,\nthat would cause an immediate currency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794674,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collapse\nfor 90% of economies around the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798408,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially if they lose 95%\nof their export revenue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802141,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as you can see here, the Gulf\ncurrencies look surprisingly stable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807641,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the Saudi Riyadh is nice\nand tied to the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812174,
    "dDurationMs": 567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812741,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Kuwaiti dinar is very stable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816474,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Emirati dirham"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819608,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is also extremely stable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822708,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may not look very stable like this,\nbut if you look at these numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826841,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over here, it's just tiny, tiny,\ntiny movements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830674,
    "dDurationMs": 2334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These currencies are absolutely fine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833008,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why is that the case?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834708,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it's\nbecause they are extremely wealthy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838541,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everybody knows that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839741,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how wealthy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841874,
    "dDurationMs": 1334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go back to our map."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843208,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go from north to south."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845941,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iraq has the smallest, a wealth fund"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850108,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "estimated at roughly $6 billion worth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854041,
    "dDurationMs": 2333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's tiny, but a central bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856374,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A war\nchest is actually pretty full at roughly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860441,
    "dDurationMs": 5267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "800 billion USD."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866308,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, let's go to their small\nsouthern neighbor, Kuwait."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870808,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their wealth fund is absolutely massive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875308,
    "dDurationMs": 4766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with $1 trillion in assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880308,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, its central bank only has half of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883508,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what Iraq has at 54 billion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887908,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Qatar has about $550 billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894308,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in its wealth fund\nand about 72 on top of that in reserves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900808,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, compared to that, Bahrain looks\nvery poor indeed, with only 17 billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906108,
    "dDurationMs": 5266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in its wealth fund and just 4 billion\nin central bank reserves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911908,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saudi Arabia, the giant, is surprisingly\nnot the richest country."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916641,
    "dDurationMs": 1967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's famous wealth funds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918608,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The piss has an estimated 1"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922441,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trillion,\nso still way, way more than Bahrain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926508,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In its assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928208,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the central bank has about 500"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931374,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion in reserves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934508,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And next the UAE is surprisingly richer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938674,
    "dDurationMs": 4634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has about 2 trillion\nin all of its wealth funds combined,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943308,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then about 227"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946341,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion in the central bank reserves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950808,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, me drawing these numbers\non the screen by themselves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954608,
    "dDurationMs": 1166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are meaningless, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955774,
    "dDurationMs": 934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just big numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956708,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bahrain may look poorer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958241,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it also has a much smaller population\nthan, for example, Saudi Arabia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962408,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it doesn't need to import as much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964474,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what we need to do now\nis to put all of that together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968008,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and calculate how many years\neach Gulf country can keep importing stuff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971941,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while exporting way less,\nand in some cases, almost nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976041,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this simple exercise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977408,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will actually reveal why Gulf currencies\nlook as stable as ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981808,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is,\neven if we assume, conservatively,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983908,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that only 40% of their oil funds\ncan be sold"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988241,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fairly easily without absolutely crashing\nglobal markets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992241,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We will find that Saudi\nArabia can survive actually forever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997974,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to its pipeline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001041,
    "dDurationMs": 5533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hyper exposed Kuwait also quite\nsurprisingly so 95% less export revenue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006574,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can still survive a whopping ten years\nbased on its massive wealth fund,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012074,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is almost as big as that of Saudi\nArabia, which is of course, much bigger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016341,
    "dDurationMs": 1567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qatar also very wealthy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017908,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No more exports\nalmost can survive for almost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1022874,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eight years\njust based on its massive wealth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026474,
    "dDurationMs": 5134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, the UAE can hold out\nfor about seven and a half years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032108,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "despite the destruction of Dubai's\nentire business model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035474,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to its wealth and, of course, its \npipeline and alternative harbors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040341,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041874,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iraq can hold out almost for two years,\nmostly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046874,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to now its pipeline to Turkey\nand its big central bank of artists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052074,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's only really Bahrain\nthat looks very vulnerable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056208,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being able to survive\nonly for a seven months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059941,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to its reliance on Hormuz\nand relatively small wealth funds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064608,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But honestly, Bahrain is so small\nthat Saudi Arabia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067941,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could simply bail it out if need it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071974,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unless, of course, you can goes\ntruly scorched earth on the Gulf,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076574,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bringing us to scenario number three\na disastrous war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081208,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Total war in this scenario, Iran tries\nto break Gulf economies export capacities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086908,
    "dDurationMs": 6533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by bombing their pipelines,\nwhich is, of course possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093574,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on top of that, they could really bomb"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096841,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the alternative ports that the UAE has,\nwhich are fairly close to Iran."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101941,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in that case, the UAE may become\njust as blocked as Qatar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106441,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because it is less wealthy per person,\nit would now be able to survive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112041,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a little under two years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116008,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,\nthanks to its red seaports"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119241,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all across the coast\nover there, Saudi Arabia,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122641,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if it no longer has its pipeline,\nit would still have some export capacity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126708,
    "dDurationMs": 4466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left 20%, roughly\nallowing it to hold out for about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132141,
    "dDurationMs": 1467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "five and a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133608,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "half years purely on their massive wealth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137608,
    "dDurationMs": 2533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is still quite a long time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140141,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So okay, now Iran again escalates bombing\nmajor population centers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145708,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This exposes yet another big weakness\nin the Gulf economies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149808,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "namely their massive,\nmassive reliance on immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154108,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, the UAE consists of about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157608,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "88% immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160708,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Da also 88% immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164274,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Roughly Kuwait's 70% immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168308,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, Bahrain 50 3 a.m."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171741,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running out of space to draw on.\nBut you get the point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1174474,
    "dDurationMs": 4634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Saudi Arabia way less 41% immigrants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179841,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iraq."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181208,
    "dDurationMs": 1166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It does have immigrants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182374,
    "dDurationMs": 5034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but these are mostly Syrian refugees\nwhich are less affected by this crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187441,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, if the war escalates,\na lot of these could be leaving,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192074,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going back home, often to South Asia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196008,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crashing or Britain crashing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199208,
    "dDurationMs": 1233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Gulf economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200441,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, from a pure war\neconomy perspective, the upside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203641,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would then be that the Gulf economies\nwould need a lot fewer imports,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209174,
    "dDurationMs": 2467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning that they could hold out\nquite a bit longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211641,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the war truly escalates,\nit may not be in Iran's best interest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216474,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to actually bomb all of these population\ncenters and send the immigrants home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220441,
    "dDurationMs": 2867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Honestly,\nthe only real existential weakness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223308,
    "dDurationMs": 5333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I see right now are the water\ndesalination plants, especially Qatar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229074,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bahrain, Kuwait and the UAE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233141,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rely on more than half roughly\nfor their entire water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236908,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supply on the Asian plants,\nwhich is this red bar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240941,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these are sitting ducks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244308,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for drinking water, it's even worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247308,
    "dDurationMs": 5833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "99% of Qatar's drinking water\ncomes from these plants, 90% in Bahrain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253141,
    "dDurationMs": 2567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while in Saudi Arabia it is way less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255708,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm still betting that you will see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257241,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a humanitarian disaster\nif Iran destroys them all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261241,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Entire cities would have to be evacuated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264408,
    "dDurationMs": 1233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be terrible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265641,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet again, this could\nthen also mean that the immigrants"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268408,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go home\nwhile the native population are evacuated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271641,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet then again, this could also mean\nthat the immigrants will go home while"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277241,
    "dDurationMs": 6833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the native population will be evacuated\nto further inland Saudi Arabia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1284108,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From there, they could regroup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286841,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because their central bank wealth\nand wealth funds will be unaffected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290908,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, these are global."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292408,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top of that,\nthe foundation of their economy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295608,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is their massive oil wealth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298908,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It will all still be there on the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302441,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of that infrastructure\nthen there will be lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305341,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, now could be rebuilt\nonce the Iranian regime is out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309441,
    "dDurationMs": 5133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So honestly, even in a complete disaster\nscenario, the Gulf countries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314708,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look more resilient\nthan I initially thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318874,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in conclusion, yes, the Gulf\neconomies are exceptionally exposed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324208,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this war continues,\nwe could see an economic destruction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328074,
    "dDurationMs": 2667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a truly gigantic scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330741,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the economic diversification\nefforts of Dubai, Qatar, Bahrain,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335541,
    "dDurationMs": 5233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all what they've worked for for years,\neven decades, it is now truly all at risk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340774,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And given their dependance on desalination\nplants for water, we could even see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344574,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a major humanitarian disaster\nif the war escalates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348541,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, honestly, in a true\nall out war scenario, the Gulf"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351808,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economies are less likely to collapse\nthan I thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355074,
    "dDurationMs": 1867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I first started my analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356941,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found out how much they depended\non the Strait of Hormuz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1360508,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like if you hear that your friend\njust lost his job and half his wealth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365341,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, your first reaction might be\nthat you think that he is ruined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1369708,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until you find out he still has half\nof his Ferrari collection left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374408,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that analogy\nkind of sums it up for me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378374,
    "dDurationMs": 1534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are the Gulf states."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1379908,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That being said,\nthese guys have worked for years and years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383074,
    "dDurationMs": 5234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to become a global safe haven,\nand that status is now truly under threat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388608,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dubai's entire business\nmodel looks very shaky indeed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392574,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what will happen to Saudi\nArabia's ultra expensive megaprojects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397474,
    "dDurationMs": 1634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the line?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399108,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even in our optimistic scenario,\nthe Gulf states are still facing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1402908,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a major recession,\nand it may take years for them to recover."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406974,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But perhaps even worse, if they are forced\nto start selling their wealth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1414141,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415041,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many poor\nSouth Asian immigrants are forced to leave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419741,
    "dDurationMs": 5267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Gulf states and go back home,\nwho is really in trouble?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425008,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425808,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Poor and indebted countries\nlike Egypt, Jordan,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432608,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pakistan and Bangladesh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435908,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have to do a follow up\nanalysis on that soon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439074,
    "dDurationMs": 1567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let me know if you want to see that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440641,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, there is, of course, Iran itself,\nwhich has many of the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444841,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vulnerabilities that the Gulf has its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448374,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oil also has to go\nthrough the Strait of Hormuz,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451408,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's all concentrated\non a single island."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1454608,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it also relies a lot on water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458708,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "desalination plants all across its ghosts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462108,
    "dDurationMs": 2766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And very crucially,\nit does not have the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464874,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "financial buffers\nthat the Gulf countries do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468008,
    "dDurationMs": 2266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to get a better sense of that,\nI highly recommend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470274,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you check out the excellent analysis\nby our advertising sponsor, The Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474941,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, I urge you to read this\nanalysis on how Iran is still making"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1479341,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lots of money from its oil exports\nthrough the Strait of Hormuz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483008,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on this analysis on\nhow not just the US."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486874,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, Iran still risks overplaying\nits hand by dragging the war out longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491808,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then to better understand\nthe ultimate doom scenario, I recommend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495708,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you read their take on why,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497041,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the current Gulf\nWar, water may prove as decisive as oil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1501341,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which goes into why Iran is vulnerable\nas well as these article show,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506308,
    "dDurationMs": 2766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Economist delivers insights to let"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509074,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you see the bigger picture\nand think for yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512108,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why I have almost always\nrelied on their analysis for my research,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517474,
    "dDurationMs": 1534,
